    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:20+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T04:10:20+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:20Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T17:40:20Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of WA extends a ridge over southern parts of the state while a weak trough lies across central Australia near the norther border. The high will drift over the southeast today and into the Tasman Sea on Friday, allowing a trough and low pressure system to move across SA on Friday. A brief high pressure system settles over SA on Saturday before another trough and low starts to move across from WA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW005" description="Lower South East" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. The chance of fog early this morning. Light winds. Daytime maximum temperatures between 19 and 22.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny morning. Medium chance of showers in the evening. Light winds becoming northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then tending northerly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 9 with daytime temperatures reaching the high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning. Winds northerly 15 to 25 km/h shifting west to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning then becoming westerly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers. Winds westerly 15 to 25 km/h tending southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
